      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 810 nm STED nanoscopy setup and an appropriate combination of two fluorescent dyes (Si-rhodamine 680SiR and carbopyronine 610CP) have been developed for near-IR live-cell super-resolution imaging. Vimentin endogenously tagged using the CRISPR/Cas9 approach with the SNAP tag, together with a noncovalent tubulin label, provided reliable and cell-to-cell reproducible dual-color confocal and STED imaging of the cytoskeleton in living cells."},
